Rules:
  [P1] Use Laravel or Symfony framework.
  [P2] Use dependency injection.
  [P3] Use Eloquent ORM or Doctrine.
  [P4] Use repositories for data access.
  [P5] Use services for business logic.
  [P6] Use form requests for validation.
  [P7] Use resource classes for API responses.
  [P8] Use events and listeners for decoupling.

Pros:
  - Rapid development
  - Large ecosystem
  - Good documentation

Cons:
  - Magic behavior
  - Performance overhead
  - Learning curve

Alternatives:
  - Go (simpler)
  - Node.js (JS everywhere)
  - Python (cleaner)

State: +

